.TH UP 1 "2026-11" "paw-proxy" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
up \- Dev server wrapper — register routes with paw\-proxy and run commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B up
.RB [ -n
.IR name ]
.RB [ \-\-restart ]
.RB [ \-\-tailnet ]
.I command
.RI [ args... ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B up
Dev server wrapper — register routes with paw\-proxy and run commands.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n \fIname\fR
Custom domain name (default: package.json name or directory)
.TP
.B \-\-restart
Auto\-restart on crash (non\-zero exit)
.TP
.B \-\-tailnet
Also serve on your tailnet with Tailscale Serve (falls back to .test only)
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B PORT
Allocated port for your dev server to bind to
.TP
.B APP_DOMAIN
Domain name, e.g. myapp.test
.TP
.B APP_URL
Full URL, e.g. https://myapp.test
.TP
.B HTTPS
Always "true"
.TP
.B APP_TAILNET_URL
Tailnet URL, set only when \-\-tailnet is serving
.TP
.B NODE_EXTRA_CA_CERTS
Path to CA cert (for Node.js HTTPS requests)
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Run Bun dev server with HTTPS:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ up bun dev
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run npm dev server with HTTPS:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ up npm run dev
.fi
.RE
.PP
Custom domain: https://api.test:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ up \-n api bun dev
.fi
.RE
.PP
Auto\-restart on crash:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ up \-\-restart bun dev
.fi
.RE
.PP
Also open it from your phone over Tailscale:
.PP
.RS
.nf
$ up \-\-tailnet bun dev
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paw\-proxy(1)
